# Contract fixture for scripts/check_sagebrain_contract.py (make
# sagebrain-contract-check): binds the raw input file of sagebrain-model's worked
# pipeline example (examples/pipeline_provenance.ttl: syn27000001 -> nf-core ->
# syn27000002 -> DESeq2 -> syn26999999, which association:apoe-expr-samp01 in
# examples/AD-cohort.ttl is sagebrain:derived_from) to this repo's example Access
# Requirement (govid:ar/42, plans/model_refactor.md's new-namespace IRI -- the
# curated record and the graph node share it, R5), so the joined worked example
# has a governed source whose ControlLabel must reach the Association.
# Illustrative, not real Synapse data.
#
# syn:syn27000001 is typed and given a benefactor here, conforming to
# shape:SynapseEntityShape's closed shape (shapes/governance.shacl.ttl) --
# sagebrain-model's own examples/pipeline_provenance.ttl types it only under the
# old gov: namespace (https://sagebionetworks.org/governance/, its own pinned
# import), a different IRI from this repo's current gov:SynapseEntity
# (https://w3id.org/synapse/governance#SynapseEntity) that carries no SHACL
# obligations of its own here.
@prefix gov: <https://w3id.org/synapse/governance#> .
@prefix govid: <https://w3id.org/synapse/governance/> .
@prefix syn: <https://www.synapse.org/Synapse:> .

syn:syn27000001 a gov:SynapseEntity ;
    gov:benefactor syn:syn27000001 ;
    gov:requiresAR govid:ar/42 .

govid:ar/42 a gov:AccessRequirement ;
    gov:dataTier gov:ControlledTier .
